.TH b4 1  "b4 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
b4 \- Read Banking4 vault files: decrypt a vault into a DuckDB database and query it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBb4\fR [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-header\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read Banking4 vault files: decrypt a vault into a DuckDB database and query it
.PP
b4 works in two steps. `b4 decrypt` reads a Banking4 vault (.sub), asks for its password once and writes the data into a DuckDB database file. Every other command reads only that database and never needs the password, so scripts and agents can query it. To "lock" the data again, delete the database file; to refresh it, run `b4 decrypt` again.
.PP
The database is the file given with \-\-db, else the one named by the environment variable B4_DB, else ./b4.duckdb.
.PP
A vault is only ever read, never changed. Bank access data stored in a vault (logins, keys, TAN settings) is never read and never reaches the database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: ./b4.duckdb]
Database file: written by `decrypt`, read by every other command
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBB4_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format [default: table]

table is made for reading: line breaks, control characters and text direction overrides in the data are replaced. csv, jsonl and json are data: written to a file or a pipe they are exact, byte for byte. Only when they are written to a terminal are the characters a terminal acts on (escape sequences, text direction overrides) made harmless: csv shows U+FFFD in their place, json and jsonl write them as \\uXXXX escapes.

In json and jsonl a number that a double cannot hold exactly is a string of its digits: an integer beyond 2^53, a decimal of more than 15 significant digits.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Aligned text, fitted to the terminal
.IP \(bu 2
json: One JSON array of objects
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl: One JSON object per line
.IP \(bu 2
csv: Comma\-separated values with a header line
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-header\fR
Leave out the header line of table and csv output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Do not print informational messages to stderr

Silences progress and summary lines and the "no rows" note. Warnings and errors are still printed.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
b4\-decrypt(1)
Decrypt a vault into a DuckDB database
.TP
b4\-info(1)
Show a vault\*(Aqs header without the password
.TP
b4\-status(1)
Describe the database and whether it is stale
.TP
b4\-accounts(1)
List and show accounts
.TP
b4\-bookings(1)
List, show and sum up bookings
.TP
b4\-payees(1)
List payees
.TP
b4\-categories(1)
List categories
.TP
b4\-standing\-orders(1)
List standing orders
.TP
b4\-portfolio(1)
List securities positions
.TP
b4\-sql(1)
Run a read\-only SQL query against the database
.TP
b4\-schema(1)
List tables and columns with their descriptions
.TP
b4\-export(1)
Export tables to files, one file per table
.TP
b4\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
b4 decrypt \(ti/Banking/Household.sub
    Ask for the vault password and write ./b4.duckdb.
b4 accounts list
    List the accounts in the database.
b4 bookings list \-\-account giro \-\-from 2025\-01 \-\-filter supermarkt
    Search the bookings of one account since January 2025.
b4 bookings summary \-\-by category \-\-from 2025 \-\-output json
    Sum up the bookings since 2025 per category, as JSON.
b4 sql \(aqselect count(*) from bookings\(aq
    Run any read\-only SQL query.
rm b4.duckdb
    Lock again: the decrypted copy is gone, the vault is untouched.
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.nf
B4_DB        The database file, as with \-\-db.
B4_PASSWORD  The vault password for \(gab4 decrypt\(ga. Other processes of the
             same user can read it; \(gab4 decrypt \-\-help\(ga names better ways.
B4_ASKPASS   A program that asks for the vault password when \(gab4 decrypt\(ga
             has no terminal, as SSH_ASKPASS does for ssh.
SSH_ASKPASS  Used in its place in a graphical session when B4_ASKPASS is
             not set, unless SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE is \(ganever\(ga.
NO_COLOR     When set, the \(gaerror:\(ga prefix is not coloured.
.fi
